 identification of domain isotypes in pfam data
Message-ID: <169051913125.2637092.1593863700763787778.reportbug@sputnik>

Package: wnpp
Severity: wishlist

Subject: ITP: r-bioc-pfamanalyzer -- GNU R identification of domain isotypes in pfam data
Package: wnpp
Owner: Andreas Tille <tille at debian.org>
Severity: wishlist

* Package name    : r-bioc-pfamanalyzer
  Version         : 1.0.1
  Upstream Author : Kristoffer Vitting-Seerup
* URL             : https://bioconductor.org/packages/pfamAnalyzeR/
* License         : MIT
  Programming Lang: GNU R
  Description     : GNU R identification of domain isotypes in pfam data
 Protein domains is one of the most import annoation of proteins we have
 with the Pfam database/tool being (by far) the most used tool. This R
 package enables the user to read the pfam prediction from both webserver
 and stand-alone runs into R. We have recently shown most human protein
 domains exist as multiple distinct variants termed domain isotypes.
 Different domain isotypes are used in a cell, tissue, and disease-
 specific manner. Accordingly, we find that domain isotypes, compared to
 each other, modulate, or abolish the functionality of a protein domain.
 This R package enables the identification and classification of such
 domain isotypes from Pfam data.

Remark: This package is maintained by Debian R Packages Maintainers at
   https://salsa.debian.org/r-pkg-team/r-bioc-pfamanalyzer


